1
00:00:02,068 --> 00:00:05,672
<i>This is the story of
a maverick female doctor.</i>

2
00:00:06,773 --> 00:00:11,311
<i>In 2019, the ivory towers are
completely crumbling.</i>

3
00:00:12,012 --> 00:00:14,080
With the arrest
of Assistant Director Tange,

4
00:00:14,147 --> 00:00:16,616
there are rumors
that there will be a purge.

5
00:00:17,550 --> 00:00:20,487
You mean three department heads
will get canned?

6
00:00:20,587 --> 00:00:25,492
Tange faction, Doctors Ushio
and Hamachi are sure to go.

7
00:00:25,592 --> 00:00:28,194
What about Dr. Hara?
Was he already canned?

8
00:00:29,662 --> 00:00:33,500
Apparently, he took time off to see
a concert in Hokkaido.

9
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:35,835
<i>- It's Yuji Kudo.
- A Yu concert?</i>

10
00:00:36,102 --> 00:00:38,238
How can he be so carefree
at a time like this?

11
00:00:45,845 --> 00:00:50,183
<i>Japan's university hospitals have
fallen into tremendous debt.</i>

12
00:00:50,450 --> 00:00:52,719
<i>Lifesaving medical treatment</i>

13
00:00:53,219 --> 00:00:56,790
<i>has entered the era of
financial jungle law.</i>

14
00:00:59,559 --> 00:01:01,761
This incident
with Assistant Director Tange is

15
00:01:03,630 --> 00:01:08,268
a truly regrettable affair.

16
00:01:08,635 --> 00:01:12,072
For the time being,
Totei University Hospital is

17
00:01:12,138 --> 00:01:14,541
sure to be buffeted with controversy.

18
00:01:15,141 --> 00:01:18,678
The Totei University Rebirth Plan 2020,

19
00:01:19,312 --> 00:01:24,384
the reforms he cajoled us
into implementing,

20
00:01:24,451 --> 00:01:26,419
I am partly responsible for.

21
00:01:26,786 --> 00:01:31,491
Therefore, I have determined
that I will take the helm.

22
00:01:32,759 --> 00:01:34,727
What about all of you?

23
00:01:35,395 --> 00:01:37,230
Are you willing to follow me?

24
00:01:37,730 --> 00:01:39,532
Yes, sir!

25
00:01:42,335 --> 00:01:44,437
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

26
00:01:46,372 --> 00:01:48,341
TOTEI UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL
REBIRTH PLAN 2020

27
00:01:48,441 --> 00:01:51,578
- Director Kaji.
- Yes?

28
00:01:51,911 --> 00:01:55,381
- Director Ushio.
- Yes?

29
00:01:55,448 --> 00:01:58,618
- Director Hamachi.
- Yes?

30
00:02:00,386 --> 00:02:05,091
You became directors under
Assistant Director Tange.

31
00:02:05,525 --> 00:02:08,995
I would like to know your feelings now.

32
00:02:09,095 --> 00:02:11,131
Would you please display for us

33
00:02:11,231 --> 00:02:13,500
proof of your loyalty to Director Hiruma?

34
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:15,535
Step on his picture?

35
00:02:15,602 --> 00:02:17,504
You must be kidding.

36
00:02:17,604 --> 00:02:22,108
<i>Meanwhile, this freelance maverick doctor,
who was never part of</i>

37
00:02:22,675 --> 00:02:26,779
<i>a university medical department,
showed up.</i>

38
00:02:27,280 --> 00:02:31,484
Hey! How long is this conference
going to last?

39
00:02:31,818 --> 00:02:34,220
I have an operation,
but I don't have an assistant.

40
00:02:34,287 --> 00:02:36,356
Daimon, we're having
an important discussion.

41
00:02:36,422 --> 00:02:38,158
Stay out of this, Daimon. I mean it.

42
00:02:38,224 --> 00:02:39,292
Out of my way!

43
00:02:39,425 --> 00:02:40,560
Sorry.

44
00:02:44,697 --> 00:02:48,701
I'm sorry. My apologies.
Please forgive me.

45
00:02:49,068 --> 00:02:50,537
Did you step on him?

46
00:02:54,140 --> 00:02:55,441
What are you doing?

47
00:03:07,353 --> 00:03:10,056
- Isn't that...
- No way! Nakamari?

48
00:03:12,058 --> 00:03:15,261
Thank you for returning, Dr. Nakayama.

49
00:03:15,395 --> 00:03:18,531
- It's been a while, Dr. Hiruma.
- Yes, it has.

50
00:03:19,132 --> 00:03:22,569
I don't think I need to introduce you,

51
00:03:22,635 --> 00:03:26,606
but this is Maria Nakayama,
Miss Totei University 2001,

52
00:03:26,673 --> 00:03:30,076
the first from
the university's medical school.

53
00:03:30,376 --> 00:03:32,779
Even at Boston Harvard
Medical University Hospital,

54
00:03:33,479 --> 00:03:35,815
she was a talented surgeon
who was known as

55
00:03:36,049 --> 00:03:39,152
a princess who never fails.

56
00:03:39,586 --> 00:03:42,121
A princess who never fails?

57
00:03:42,388 --> 00:03:44,257
Starting today,

58
00:03:44,324 --> 00:03:49,762
Nakayama will be joining
the Totei University medical staff.

59
00:03:51,598 --> 00:03:55,635
I'd like all of you to learn from
her excellent career.

60
00:03:55,735 --> 00:03:56,836
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

61
00:04:01,241 --> 00:04:05,144
I am Maria Nakayama.
I am honored to meet all of you.

62
00:04:06,145 --> 00:04:07,413
- Yes, ma'am!
- Yes, ma'am!

63
00:04:11,251 --> 00:04:14,554
It's so nice to hear that you have
successfully completed

64
00:04:14,621 --> 00:04:17,724
so many difficult surgeries in the US.

65
00:04:17,790 --> 00:04:20,093
I have become what I am today

66
00:04:20,693 --> 00:04:23,396
- all thanks to you, Dr. Hiruma.
- Really?

67
00:04:24,264 --> 00:04:26,699
Even my title of Miss Totei University.

68
00:04:30,570 --> 00:04:33,439
You mean,
you have that kind of relationship?

69
00:04:33,506 --> 00:04:34,741
Ebina.

70
00:04:35,508 --> 00:04:38,044
Don't go asking idiotic questions.

71
00:04:40,480 --> 00:04:42,515
RURI IKURA,
SECRETARY TO THE HOSPITAL DIRECTOR

72
00:04:42,582 --> 00:04:43,549
Mistress.

73
00:04:44,284 --> 00:04:48,254
Can I put my desk next to yours,
Dr. Hiruma?

74
00:04:48,321 --> 00:04:49,622
- You mean here?
- Yes.

75
00:04:49,722 --> 00:04:51,824
I can't fit in with
the Japanese medical staff system.

76
00:04:52,091 --> 00:04:54,227
I see. Then I'll move this desk--

77
00:05:21,621 --> 00:05:25,792
Why don't we call this a draw?
You're fighting, right?

78
00:05:27,260 --> 00:05:28,461
I'm so envious.

79
00:05:29,262 --> 00:05:31,597
Dang! She's so crazy cute.

80
00:05:31,664 --> 00:05:34,300
I decided to go to Totei University
when I saw this.

81
00:05:34,400 --> 00:05:35,368
Me too!

82
00:05:35,468 --> 00:05:38,371
I bet a ton of doctors' futures were
decided by this photo.

83
00:05:38,438 --> 00:05:39,605
You bet!

84
00:05:39,806 --> 00:05:42,175
Compared to her, this one...

85
00:05:42,241 --> 00:05:43,676
- Sorry!
- No way!

86
00:05:43,810 --> 00:05:46,212
It's the difference between
an angel and a demon.

87
00:05:47,613 --> 00:05:49,615
That feels nice.

88
00:05:49,682 --> 00:05:53,319
Everyone, it's good to meet you.

89
00:05:53,519 --> 00:05:55,254
- Nice to meet you!
- Nice to meet you!

90
00:06:00,159 --> 00:06:03,363
Dr. Ushio, it's been a while.

91
00:06:04,430 --> 00:06:06,099
- Yes, it has.
- What?

92
00:06:06,165 --> 00:06:09,635
- Dr. Ushio, you know Dr. Nakayama?
- Yes.

93
00:06:09,969 --> 00:06:13,306
During my residency,
I worked with Dr. Ushio.

94
00:06:14,540 --> 00:06:16,542
That's so unfair, Dr. Ushio.

95
00:06:16,609 --> 00:06:18,444
- Unfair? What for?
- Sorry.

96
00:06:21,280 --> 00:06:23,015
Back up!

97
00:06:25,518 --> 00:06:29,555
Senior Daimon, since we're both
women doctors, let's get along.

98
00:06:29,622 --> 00:06:32,725
I decline. I'm not your senior either.

99
00:06:33,292 --> 00:06:35,695
Dang! You sure are petty.

100
00:06:35,795 --> 00:06:39,198
When a pretty woman comes along,
you're the kind that teases--

101
00:06:39,298 --> 00:06:40,800
It's all right.

102
00:06:41,367 --> 00:06:43,669
Dr. Daimon, you're a part-timer, right?

103
00:06:44,437 --> 00:06:46,205
I'm a freelancer.

104
00:06:50,309 --> 00:06:53,312
What is it? You look frightening.

105
00:07:00,253 --> 00:07:02,054
What are you doing, Dr. Daimon?

106
00:07:02,989 --> 00:07:04,690
I'm going to lunch.

107
00:07:08,394 --> 00:07:13,633
<i>This woman hates groups, authority,</i>

108
00:07:13,699 --> 00:07:15,168
<i>and restrictions.</i>

109
00:07:15,535 --> 00:07:18,771
<i>Her specialized medical license
and well-honed skills</i>

110
00:07:19,071 --> 00:07:20,473
<i>are her weapons.</i>

111
00:07:20,540 --> 00:07:23,242
I heard a famous woman doctor
from America is here.

112
00:07:23,342 --> 00:07:25,011
Was she Miss Totei University?

113
00:07:25,077 --> 00:07:26,379
Let me see her!

114
00:07:26,446 --> 00:07:28,681
Dr. Nakayama sure is popular.

115
00:07:28,781 --> 00:07:32,084
My stomach hurts.
Can I see Dr. Nakayama right away?

116
00:07:38,090 --> 00:07:40,493
Out of the way! Move!

117
00:07:41,394 --> 00:07:42,595
I'm going to feel here.

118
00:07:43,029 --> 00:07:44,197
That hurts!

119
00:07:44,263 --> 00:07:46,699
Acute abdomen. Possible ileus.
Get a stretcher.

120
00:07:47,533 --> 00:07:49,635
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon,</i>

121
00:07:49,702 --> 00:07:52,638
<i>otherwise known as Doctor X.</i>

122
00:08:21,467 --> 00:08:23,135
- First assistant.
- Yes?

123
00:08:23,436 --> 00:08:25,104
Have you done
the infectious disease check?

124
00:08:25,171 --> 00:08:27,573
- Yes, it's all clear.
- What's his blood type?

125
00:08:29,242 --> 00:08:31,110
Sorry, I haven't checked.

126
00:08:31,177 --> 00:08:32,678
- You haven't?
- I'm sorry.

127
00:08:32,745 --> 00:08:34,514
- Hop to it, Tako!
- I'm sorry.

128
00:08:34,747 --> 00:08:36,782
Could you do that immediately, please?

129
00:08:37,016 --> 00:08:38,718
- Okay.
- Thank you.

130
00:08:43,155 --> 00:08:47,193
Dr. Daimon, I will perform the surgery.

131
00:08:47,260 --> 00:08:48,361
Why?

132
00:08:48,628 --> 00:08:50,463
He is my patient.

133
00:08:51,564 --> 00:08:53,299
What are you talking about?

134
00:08:53,399 --> 00:08:55,201
I'm doing this. Out of the way.

135
00:08:57,403 --> 00:08:59,338
- Dr. Tako.
- Yes?

136
00:08:59,805 --> 00:09:02,108
Please, help me.

137
00:09:03,709 --> 00:09:05,077
- Yes, ma'am!
- Yes, ma'am!

138
00:09:07,046 --> 00:09:08,848
Dr. Daimon, don't interfere.

139
00:09:08,915 --> 00:09:10,583
- You're in the way, Dr. Daimon.
- Out of the way!

140
00:09:10,650 --> 00:09:12,251
- Stand back!
- That hurts!

141
00:09:12,351 --> 00:09:13,553
You're in the way!

142
00:09:15,488 --> 00:09:17,290
What the heck is going on here?

143
00:09:20,059 --> 00:09:21,994
Thank you.

144
00:09:22,461 --> 00:09:23,462
What are his vitals?

145
00:09:23,696 --> 00:09:29,735
BP, 118 over 73. Pulse, 98, sinus.
Any questions?

146
00:09:31,070 --> 00:09:34,407
We will now conduct an emergency
ileus removal procedure.

147
00:09:34,507 --> 00:09:36,442
- Let us begin.
- Yes, ma'am.

148
00:09:36,509 --> 00:09:39,278
Good timing. They're just starting.

149
00:09:40,046 --> 00:09:42,448
What?
The surgeon is Miss Totei University!

150
00:09:42,515 --> 00:09:43,683
- Scalpel.
- What's the operation?

151
00:09:43,749 --> 00:09:44,684
Here.

152
00:09:55,027 --> 00:09:56,062
Here.

153
00:10:03,336 --> 00:10:05,004
Next, the peritonectomy.

154
00:10:05,137 --> 00:10:07,773
Dr. Tako, would you like to do it?

155
00:10:08,074 --> 00:10:09,775
What? I can?

156
00:10:10,176 --> 00:10:12,478
It's good learning experience.
I'll guide you.

157
00:10:14,213 --> 00:10:15,548
Thank you.

158
00:10:20,019 --> 00:10:23,089
- Coopers and hooked forceps.
- Here.

159
00:10:27,493 --> 00:10:30,229
She let the young surgeon take over
and is guiding him.

160
00:10:30,363 --> 00:10:32,331
What a model surgeon.

161
00:10:32,732 --> 00:10:36,068
That's totally different than that
demon who does everything herself.

162
00:10:36,802 --> 00:10:39,205
I can sense her generosity.

163
00:10:44,377 --> 00:10:46,812
Cut the band
that's constricting the ileum.

164
00:10:47,513 --> 00:10:51,283
- Okay. Metzenbaum scissors.
- Here.

165
00:10:57,757 --> 00:11:00,626
- Very good.
- This is awesome.

166
00:11:03,329 --> 00:11:06,732
- Remove the constriction.
- Okay.

167
00:11:08,267 --> 00:11:12,471
Nakamari is there?
I wish I had been in the operating room.

168
00:11:12,738 --> 00:11:14,373
Maria Nakayama.

169
00:11:14,507 --> 00:11:18,044
She's also called the legendary
pin-up woman doctor.

170
00:11:18,110 --> 00:11:19,612
What? A pin-up doctor?

171
00:11:19,679 --> 00:11:23,416
She's been on the cover of
many medical magazines.

172
00:11:23,482 --> 00:11:28,821
<i>The World Doctors. Surgery Weekly.
Lovely Patient.</i>

173
00:11:29,088 --> 00:11:30,256
<i>And it's not just covers.</i>

174
00:11:30,322 --> 00:11:33,693
She's also successfully completed
numerous complex surgeries,

175
00:11:33,759 --> 00:11:36,328
and her papers have received high praise.

176
00:11:36,429 --> 00:11:39,432
Really? I can't believe it. That's <i>pon!</i>

177
00:11:39,498 --> 00:11:40,633
<i>Pon!</i>

178
00:11:40,733 --> 00:11:46,572
She's pretty amazing. She's also
operated with Professor MacArthur.

179
00:11:46,639 --> 00:11:49,842
Really? Isn't Professor MacArthur
the one who won the Nobel Prize?

180
00:11:50,142 --> 00:11:52,478
That's right. And it's not just MacArthur.

181
00:11:52,545 --> 00:11:55,448
She's also operated with
Professors Charlin and Starchill.

182
00:11:55,581 --> 00:12:00,486
That means she's so good that even
world-famous doctors recognize her.

183
00:12:00,786 --> 00:12:04,657
Unbelievable. That's <i>pon</i> too!

184
00:12:04,757 --> 00:12:08,060
She's young, feminine, and pleasant.

185
00:12:08,160 --> 00:12:11,564
That's all the things that
Ms. Daimon isn't.

186
00:12:11,630 --> 00:12:14,200
- That's for sure.
- What?

187
00:12:14,300 --> 00:12:16,669
- That's it!
- I'm right?

188
00:12:17,503 --> 00:12:18,771
<i>Pon.</i>

189
00:12:20,139 --> 00:12:22,274
You're just waiting for the final tile.

190
00:12:23,242 --> 00:12:27,480
- Which one should I choose?
- Just do it.

191
00:12:28,414 --> 00:12:31,117
- This one!
- What is it? I can't see!

192
00:12:31,183 --> 00:12:34,220
- There it is! Congratulations!
- Thank you!

193
00:12:34,487 --> 00:12:36,889
<i>Ron! Mangan!</i>

194
00:12:44,096 --> 00:12:47,399
With all your success in the US,
why did you come back to Japan?

195
00:12:48,834 --> 00:12:51,303
I couldn't forget you, Dr. Ushio.

196
00:12:51,670 --> 00:12:53,205
That's a lie.

197
00:12:53,539 --> 00:12:54,774
You dumped me.

198
00:12:56,709 --> 00:12:58,611
I understood after going to America.

199
00:13:04,450 --> 00:13:07,219
I want to operate with you again,
Dr. Ushio.

200
00:13:09,121 --> 00:13:12,525
Wait.
Isn't that Dr. Ushio and Dr. Nakayama?

201
00:13:12,591 --> 00:13:16,228
Did you know that she was
Director Hiruma's mistress?

202
00:13:16,295 --> 00:13:18,164
Now she's going after Dr. Ushio too?

203
00:13:22,168 --> 00:13:23,202
Is that right?

204
00:13:23,269 --> 00:13:25,304
What a total enchantress.

205
00:13:25,471 --> 00:13:27,740
You better be careful of her,
Dr. Murasaki.

206
00:13:28,808 --> 00:13:30,442
She's frightening.

207
00:13:31,811 --> 00:13:33,112
That's delicious.

208
00:13:35,514 --> 00:13:37,483
Well, Representative Hachimura.

209
00:13:37,616 --> 00:13:40,286
Welcome to Totei University Hospital.

210
00:13:40,386 --> 00:13:44,824
It doesn't exactly feel good to be
welcomed to a hospital.

211
00:13:45,424 --> 00:13:47,393
Well, I couldn't agree more.

212
00:13:47,827 --> 00:13:49,361
However, Representative Hachimura,

213
00:13:49,762 --> 00:13:53,532
why didn't you
come consult with me sooner?

214
00:13:53,599 --> 00:13:55,634
I am a National Diet Member.

215
00:13:55,734 --> 00:13:58,504
The safety and security
of the citizens comes first.

216
00:13:58,704 --> 00:14:00,239
My own health means nothing.

217
00:14:00,372 --> 00:14:03,242
You really are something special.

218
00:14:03,776 --> 00:14:07,112
I'm Dr. Ushio, Director of
Next-Generation Intelligent Surgery.

219
00:14:08,247 --> 00:14:11,350
Your illness is ischemic cardiomyopathy.

220
00:14:12,184 --> 00:14:14,987
First of all,
we'll need to operate on you.

221
00:14:16,655 --> 00:14:17,990
Can I be cured?

222
00:14:18,090 --> 00:14:21,293
Representative Hachimura,
since your father's time,

223
00:14:21,794 --> 00:14:24,029
we've been taking care of the lives of

224
00:14:24,096 --> 00:14:27,032
the Hachimura family here
at Totei University Hospital.

225
00:14:27,266 --> 00:14:28,801
Please leave this to us.

226
00:14:31,103 --> 00:14:33,038
- All right. Thank you.
- You're welcome.

227
00:14:41,747 --> 00:14:43,015
Boobs.

228
00:14:43,816 --> 00:14:45,184
I'm sorry.

229
00:14:48,153 --> 00:14:51,490
In the surgery the other day,
Dr. Nakayama touched me with hers.

230
00:14:52,057 --> 00:14:54,426
Cut the band
that's constricting the ileum.

231
00:14:56,295 --> 00:14:57,296
Okay.

232
00:14:57,630 --> 00:15:00,065
I couldn't sleep that night.

233
00:15:00,532 --> 00:15:01,734
I haven't even taken a bath.

234
00:15:02,034 --> 00:15:03,302
- Seriously?
- Yes.

235
00:15:05,771 --> 00:15:07,539
- Don't smell him.
- Sorry.

236
00:15:07,640 --> 00:15:09,541
- Suction.
- I can?

237
00:15:10,776 --> 00:15:13,312
- Not that kind!
- Sorry.

238
00:15:14,380 --> 00:15:18,584
What a moron. He's pitiful.
No wonder you're a plebe.

239
00:15:18,784 --> 00:15:20,552
What a total moron.

240
00:15:24,023 --> 00:15:26,558
- Dr. Nakayama.
- Please allow me to observe.

241
00:15:28,627 --> 00:15:30,529
You sure are dedicated.

242
00:15:30,596 --> 00:15:33,599
You've got a brilliant career,
so why watch other surgeries?

243
00:15:33,666 --> 00:15:35,634
To learn from other surgeons' operations.

244
00:15:37,069 --> 00:15:39,338
It's only natural for a physician.

245
00:15:43,375 --> 00:15:44,977
Outstanding.

246
00:15:47,513 --> 00:15:49,248
- Metzenbaum scissors.
- Here.

247
00:15:49,381 --> 00:15:51,216
Dr. Ebina, deeper please.

248
00:15:51,550 --> 00:15:52,651
I can't see.

249
00:15:53,085 --> 00:15:56,722
Dr. Tako, the portal hepatis has been
blocked for over 25 minutes.

250
00:15:56,789 --> 00:15:58,424
- Hurry with the ligation.
- Right.

251
00:15:58,490 --> 00:16:00,025
- You're too slow, Tako.
- Sorry.

252
00:16:00,125 --> 00:16:01,560
- You too, Dr. Ebina.
- I know.

253
00:16:01,627 --> 00:16:02,695
I've got it.

254
00:16:02,761 --> 00:16:04,663
Tako! Ebi! You're too slow!

255
00:16:04,730 --> 00:16:07,366
- You're too fast, Daimon.
- Don't rush us.

256
00:16:07,433 --> 00:16:09,535
- Down with rushed operations!
- Then don't be slow!

257
00:16:10,369 --> 00:16:11,737
Hurry up!

258
00:16:12,204 --> 00:16:13,772
She's nothing but a bully.

259
00:16:14,139 --> 00:16:16,508
That demon never changes.

260
00:16:18,410 --> 00:16:22,114
Is Dr. Daimon simply a part-timer?

261
00:16:23,482 --> 00:16:25,117
No, she's not simply a part-timer.

262
00:16:26,185 --> 00:16:28,620
She's an ill-natured part-timer.

263
00:16:42,201 --> 00:16:45,571
- That was nice work.
- Thanks.

264
00:16:46,238 --> 00:16:47,806
Dr. Daimon.

265
00:16:49,441 --> 00:16:53,045
I was surprised at how talented
a surgeon you are.

266
00:16:54,046 --> 00:16:57,349
The next time I operate,
will you be my assistant?

267
00:16:57,716 --> 00:16:59,184
I decline.

268
00:17:00,285 --> 00:17:01,854
Why not?

269
00:17:02,121 --> 00:17:05,357
Is it because I'm a woman
and younger than you?

270
00:17:05,424 --> 00:17:09,561
No. It's because
you're a horrible surgeon.

271
00:17:15,234 --> 00:17:17,770
The prince of the political world
checked into this hospital.

272
00:17:17,936 --> 00:17:19,505
You mean, Masayoshi Hachimura?

273
00:17:20,172 --> 00:17:22,107
So what's wrong with him?

274
00:17:22,274 --> 00:17:24,043
His heart!

275
00:17:24,510 --> 00:17:28,414
Won't you allow Internal Medicine
handle Mr. Hachimura's treatment?

276
00:17:29,515 --> 00:17:32,284
Gradually heal him through medicine?

277
00:17:34,253 --> 00:17:36,755
It will take time and well...

278
00:17:37,022 --> 00:17:39,625
That's rather dull, isn't it?

279
00:17:40,159 --> 00:17:42,361
I would appreciate it

280
00:17:42,428 --> 00:17:46,065
if you did your best to follow
Surgery's lead on this one.

281
00:17:46,131 --> 00:17:49,501
Internal Medicine isn't here
just to support Surgery.

282
00:17:49,802 --> 00:17:53,072
If we can only follow their lead
at a time like this,

283
00:17:53,138 --> 00:17:56,475
then there's no point in having me
as director of Internal Medicine.

284
00:17:56,675 --> 00:17:59,278
Yes. The point in having you around...

285
00:17:59,945 --> 00:18:01,580
Where are you from again?

286
00:18:02,581 --> 00:18:05,684
- I'm from Gifu.
- Gifu? That's a nice place.

287
00:18:06,051 --> 00:18:07,986
That's where Dosan Saito is from.

288
00:18:08,120 --> 00:18:10,756
That bald guy. Nice.

289
00:18:11,757 --> 00:18:13,358
Do you want to return there?

290
00:18:14,326 --> 00:18:18,163
You see, I heard
Takayama Satellite Hospital 19 has

291
00:18:18,263 --> 00:18:21,633
a vacancy for assistant hospital director.

292
00:18:30,242 --> 00:18:32,244
<i>I am ready.</i>

293
00:18:32,578 --> 00:18:35,380
Let's begin this special conference.

294
00:18:35,547 --> 00:18:36,548
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

295
00:18:37,449 --> 00:18:41,153
The patient is Masayoshi Hachimura,
male, age 39.

296
00:18:43,222 --> 00:18:45,224
As you already know, he is the prince of

297
00:18:45,290 --> 00:18:47,326
the political world
and top candidate for next PM.

298
00:18:47,493 --> 00:18:50,028
Be particularly careful
that no trouble is caused.

299
00:18:50,129 --> 00:18:51,096
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

300
00:18:51,230 --> 00:18:53,665
He's been diagnosed with
ischemic cardiomyopathy.

301
00:18:53,765 --> 00:18:55,801
There is constriction in three
main arteries,

302
00:18:56,101 --> 00:18:57,736
including the left coronary artery.

303
00:18:58,537 --> 00:18:59,938
As for the treatment,

304
00:19:00,072 --> 00:19:02,941
due to damage to the three arteries,
catheter treatment isn't possible.

305
00:19:03,108 --> 00:19:04,710
We'll perform a low-stress

306
00:19:04,943 --> 00:19:07,613
minimally invasive beating heart
coronary artery bypass surgery.

307
00:19:08,347 --> 00:19:11,583
The AI also recommends an off-pump CABG.

308
00:19:12,084 --> 00:19:15,387
The heart's arteries will be
bypassed while the heart is pumping.

309
00:19:15,487 --> 00:19:16,989
Objection.

310
00:19:17,122 --> 00:19:18,690
His heart is weak.

311
00:19:18,991 --> 00:19:23,195
Also, it's impossible for you guys
to perform such complex surgery.

312
00:19:23,595 --> 00:19:24,730
Who said it's impossible?

313
00:19:25,364 --> 00:19:27,666
On-pump CABG.

314
00:19:27,733 --> 00:19:30,469
We'll use a heart-lung machine
and perform proven anastomosis

315
00:19:30,536 --> 00:19:32,204
to completely rebuild the arteries.

316
00:19:32,304 --> 00:19:33,605
Objection.

317
00:19:34,206 --> 00:19:38,777
In this new Reiwa era,
your methods are ancient, Dr. Daimon.

318
00:19:39,077 --> 00:19:42,214
Seventy percent of the coronary bypass
surgeries in Japan are

319
00:19:42,314 --> 00:19:44,116
off-pump CABG.

320
00:19:44,283 --> 00:19:48,287
The heart-lung machine puts immense
stress on the patient's body.

321
00:19:48,720 --> 00:19:49,721
Exactly right.

322
00:19:49,788 --> 00:19:51,557
You can tell she's been in the US.

323
00:19:51,623 --> 00:19:52,524
That's for sure.

324
00:19:52,591 --> 00:19:54,026
Therefore,

325
00:19:54,593 --> 00:19:58,497
I believe Dr. Ushio's beating heart
coronary artery bypass surgery

326
00:19:58,597 --> 00:20:00,065
is best.

327
00:20:01,733 --> 00:20:03,101
Fine.

328
00:20:03,435 --> 00:20:05,137
- Good.
- I'll do it.

329
00:20:05,304 --> 00:20:06,738
What do you mean by that?

330
00:20:07,472 --> 00:20:10,342
We can't let a part-timer operate on
the prince of the political world.

331
00:20:11,109 --> 00:20:13,478
- I'll be the surgeon.
- Seriously?

332
00:20:13,579 --> 00:20:15,380
Allow me to assist.

333
00:20:18,083 --> 00:20:20,686
- That's fine. Please do.
- Thank you.

334
00:20:20,752 --> 00:20:22,621
- I'll be second assistant!
- I'll be third assistant!

335
00:20:22,688 --> 00:20:24,289
I'll be fourth assistant!

336
00:20:24,423 --> 00:20:26,058
- I'll do anything.
- I will too!

337
00:20:26,124 --> 00:20:28,393
Please, pick me!
I'm Kurihashi, Director Ushio!

338
00:20:28,460 --> 00:20:31,230
- I'm Kanie!
- Aogi, ready to be of service!

339
00:20:31,396 --> 00:20:33,332
Please, Director Ushio!

340
00:20:33,432 --> 00:20:34,533
Director Ushio!

341
00:20:35,701 --> 00:20:39,605
Your surgery will be a beating heart
coronary artery bypass surgery.

342
00:20:39,671 --> 00:20:42,608
The AI verifies that it is
the best possible method.

343
00:20:43,242 --> 00:20:44,643
I see.

344
00:20:44,776 --> 00:20:48,213
However, I have one request.

345
00:20:50,215 --> 00:20:51,283
Yes, what is it?

346
00:20:51,416 --> 00:20:54,486
My life belongs not just to me.

347
00:20:55,053 --> 00:20:56,755
It also belongs to the citizens.

348
00:20:58,457 --> 00:20:59,491
Right.

349
00:20:59,558 --> 00:21:01,159
I'd like you to keep my illness a secret.

350
00:21:02,094 --> 00:21:03,428
I don't want to

351
00:21:03,495 --> 00:21:06,431
needlessly cause the citizens
to worry by making it public.

352
00:21:06,765 --> 00:21:08,700
You truly are amazing.

353
00:21:08,767 --> 00:21:13,705
I can see why you're next in line
to become the next prime minister.

354
00:21:13,772 --> 00:21:15,574
So admirable.

355
00:21:17,242 --> 00:21:18,810
- Are you sure?
- What?

356
00:21:20,345 --> 00:21:22,648
Don't you believe that
making your illness public is

357
00:21:23,081 --> 00:21:25,417
the proper thing for a politician to do?

358
00:21:27,185 --> 00:21:31,189
Showing the citizens how you are
battling your disease would

359
00:21:31,523 --> 00:21:34,660
give courage and hope to others who are

360
00:21:34,760 --> 00:21:37,462
similarly suffering from disease.

361
00:21:38,563 --> 00:21:40,065
That's what I believe.

362
00:21:41,133 --> 00:21:42,834
- Dr. Nakayama.
- Cut that out.

363
00:21:43,402 --> 00:21:44,736
You're the assistant here.

364
00:21:44,836 --> 00:21:46,672
- I'm terribly sorry.
- It's okay.

365
00:21:48,407 --> 00:21:49,841
- I see the light.
- What?

366
00:21:51,843 --> 00:21:55,113
I was wrong.

367
00:21:57,716 --> 00:21:58,684
Excuse me?

368
00:22:04,656 --> 00:22:10,629
I would like to thank you all for
gathering here for me today.

369
00:22:13,465 --> 00:22:15,200
This is a hospital press conference.

370
00:22:15,534 --> 00:22:20,539
I would like to straightforwardly
and openly make this announcement.

371
00:22:21,306 --> 00:22:24,576
The illness that I am now battling is

372
00:22:25,143 --> 00:22:27,145
ischemic cardiomyopathy.

373
00:22:28,146 --> 00:22:33,352
The doctors say that
my condition is extremely serious.

374
00:22:35,487 --> 00:22:38,290
I am announcing it like this

375
00:22:39,091 --> 00:22:45,497
in order to encourage myself
for the coming battle I will face.

376
00:22:47,799 --> 00:22:51,370
I will not be defeated.

377
00:22:51,436 --> 00:22:54,306
I promise you, I will survive.

378
00:22:55,807 --> 00:22:58,343
Please wait for me to return.

379
00:23:00,245 --> 00:23:02,481
I am Hospital Director Hiruma.

380
00:23:02,581 --> 00:23:05,717
I would like to announce
the surgeon for this operation.

381
00:23:06,385 --> 00:23:08,553
The surgeon will be...

382
00:23:11,056 --> 00:23:15,260
Dr. Maria Nakayama.

383
00:23:23,668 --> 00:23:27,038
What? I thought the surgeon was Dr. Ushio.

384
00:23:27,105 --> 00:23:29,241
How come Dr. Nakayama is doing it instead?

385
00:23:30,108 --> 00:23:31,810
HACHIMURA CALLS FOR
AN EMERGENCY PRESS CONFERENCE

386
00:23:33,378 --> 00:23:35,147
I am the surgeon, Dr. Nakayama.

387
00:23:36,314 --> 00:23:39,384
I swear that my operation on
Representative Hachimura

388
00:23:39,684 --> 00:23:42,554
will be successful.

389
00:23:45,023 --> 00:23:46,825
Thank you, Dr. Nakayama.

390
00:23:47,359 --> 00:23:49,227
I trust you.

391
00:23:55,167 --> 00:23:56,101
Hello.

392
00:23:56,568 --> 00:23:58,103
Citizens of Japan,

393
00:23:58,203 --> 00:24:01,406
you'll next be seeing
Representative Hachimura

394
00:24:01,540 --> 00:24:05,610
when he's released from the hospital
after his successful surgery.

395
00:24:05,744 --> 00:24:07,345
- Representative, look this way, please.
- Okay.

396
00:24:09,147 --> 00:24:10,248
- This way, please.
- Okay.

397
00:24:11,283 --> 00:24:13,285
- Over here too, please.
- Sure.

398
00:24:14,052 --> 00:24:15,287
This way, please.

399
00:24:16,488 --> 00:24:17,589
It's like we're celebrities.

400
00:24:25,030 --> 00:24:26,731
Dr. Daimon.

401
00:24:28,066 --> 00:24:31,203
I will be the surgeon in
Mr. Hachimura's surgery.

402
00:24:32,437 --> 00:24:35,774
I told you, you shouldn't operate
since you're so bad at it.

403
00:24:36,041 --> 00:24:39,811
It's okay.
I may be awful, but I never fail.

404
00:24:42,414 --> 00:24:45,150
I know a spell for never failing.

405
00:24:46,485 --> 00:24:47,486
A spell?

406
00:24:47,552 --> 00:24:52,724
It's a very effective spell
that you can't use, Dr. Daimon.

407
00:24:53,825 --> 00:24:55,227
Just you watch.

408
00:25:00,398 --> 00:25:01,533
Why?

409
00:25:02,067 --> 00:25:03,735
Why did you make Dr. Nakayama the surgeon?

410
00:25:04,035 --> 00:25:07,072
She did request it,

411
00:25:07,272 --> 00:25:09,741
but the ultimate decision was mine.

412
00:25:10,509 --> 00:25:12,777
You believe I'm less capable than
Dr. Nakayama?

413
00:25:13,078 --> 00:25:15,447
No. I'm not saying that at all.

414
00:25:15,514 --> 00:25:18,717
What you're less capable in isn't surgery,

415
00:25:19,217 --> 00:25:22,754
- but... How can I put this? Impact.
- Impact?

416
00:25:23,054 --> 00:25:25,390
She's a former Miss Totei University,

417
00:25:25,457 --> 00:25:29,127
and she's famous for
successfully completing

418
00:25:29,261 --> 00:25:32,297
numerous complex surgeries in the US.

419
00:25:32,631 --> 00:25:34,766
The Totei University princess

420
00:25:35,133 --> 00:25:38,203
saving the prince of
the political world...

421
00:25:38,303 --> 00:25:41,640
That's the kind of thing
society wants to see.

422
00:25:42,240 --> 00:25:46,211
Dr. Ushio, as the first assistant,

423
00:25:46,378 --> 00:25:49,147
- I want you to support this drama.
- I refuse!

424
00:25:49,347 --> 00:25:51,816
I will not be her assistant.

425
00:25:52,117 --> 00:25:54,553
I understand your pride, Dr. Ushio.

426
00:25:54,619 --> 00:25:57,155
- Just try to overcome--
- I'm sorry.

427
00:25:58,523 --> 00:25:59,624
Goodbye.

428
00:26:07,632 --> 00:26:09,534
He turned us down, I see.

429
00:26:10,068 --> 00:26:12,003
He sure is petty.

430
00:26:19,544 --> 00:26:22,213
Are you still doing that, Ms. Daimon?
Let's play.

431
00:26:22,280 --> 00:26:24,015
Sorry. Hold on a little longer.

432
00:26:26,351 --> 00:26:30,221
I wonder what you're looking at
so intently.

433
00:26:31,122 --> 00:26:33,692
Oh, a heart?
The prince of the political world's?

434
00:26:34,159 --> 00:26:35,794
That's not it.

435
00:26:36,294 --> 00:26:39,164
"Corrected transposition
of great arteries"?

436
00:26:39,230 --> 00:26:40,765
That's rare.

437
00:26:41,032 --> 00:26:44,402
The former Miss Totei University is
doing the prince's surgery, right?

438
00:26:44,502 --> 00:26:46,771
- That's right.
- She sure pulled some strings.

439
00:26:47,105 --> 00:26:50,308
She stole the surgery away from
Dr. Ushio at the last moment.

440
00:26:50,575 --> 00:26:53,445
She's a totally awful surgeon though.

441
00:26:59,484 --> 00:27:01,519
<i>She had to start over.</i>

442
00:27:01,753 --> 00:27:03,355
Start over?

443
00:27:03,421 --> 00:27:05,991
Are you sure that surgery will be okay?

444
00:27:06,124 --> 00:27:08,693
But she says that even though

445
00:27:08,760 --> 00:27:13,164
she's no good,
she has a spell for never failing.

446
00:27:13,298 --> 00:27:15,166
"A spell for never failing"?

447
00:27:15,667 --> 00:27:18,703
What the heck is that? Abracadabra?

448
00:27:19,004 --> 00:27:20,572
What's "Abracadabra"?

449
00:27:20,772 --> 00:27:23,441
It's supposed to be a spell
for turning you into anything.

450
00:27:23,675 --> 00:27:25,310
A neighbor often did it.

451
00:27:25,377 --> 00:27:28,613
You mean she says a spell like,
"I'll be a doctor who never fails"?

452
00:27:29,347 --> 00:27:31,516
- Don't be silly!
- Of course not!

453
00:27:31,683 --> 00:27:33,985
- You must have stiff shoulders.
- Oh, cut it out.

454
00:27:34,352 --> 00:27:36,054
Look who's here!

455
00:27:36,454 --> 00:27:37,555
Good evening.

456
00:27:37,622 --> 00:27:40,358
How about some Yokohama <i>shumai?</i>

457
00:27:44,195 --> 00:27:48,366
You know, I was a doctor who had
the best of everything.

458
00:27:49,067 --> 00:27:52,337
An elite husband. Two perfect sons.

459
00:27:52,704 --> 00:27:54,773
A large house in Yokohama with a garden.

460
00:27:57,142 --> 00:27:58,543
- She's crying.
- She's crying.

461
00:28:00,845 --> 00:28:02,347
But I didn't have it all.

462
00:28:03,214 --> 00:28:07,318
I found something in my life
that isn't the best.

463
00:28:07,585 --> 00:28:09,154
Two at once.

464
00:28:10,188 --> 00:28:11,556
What are they?

465
00:28:11,656 --> 00:28:13,391
One is my boss.

466
00:28:13,658 --> 00:28:18,096
I never thought Nicholas
would be arrested.

467
00:28:18,163 --> 00:28:20,532
He wasn't the best boss, not at all.

468
00:28:20,765 --> 00:28:23,368
Naturally, neither is Director Hiruma.

469
00:28:24,703 --> 00:28:26,404
So what's the other?

470
00:28:26,771 --> 00:28:28,139
Youth.

471
00:28:28,339 --> 00:28:29,374
Youth?

472
00:28:29,541 --> 00:28:32,043
She may be the princess of
Totei University,

473
00:28:32,310 --> 00:28:34,212
but she's fawned over
just for being young.

474
00:28:34,713 --> 00:28:37,682
I can't stand to work at
the same place that floozy does!

475
00:28:39,584 --> 00:28:41,419
- She's crying again.
- She sure cries a lot.

476
00:28:43,221 --> 00:28:46,591
I know. Would you hire me here?

477
00:28:46,791 --> 00:28:47,792
What?

478
00:28:48,159 --> 00:28:51,763
I mean, I'm confident I can become
a great freelance doctor.

479
00:28:52,063 --> 00:28:56,034
Just watch. Abracadabra!

480
00:28:56,101 --> 00:28:59,537
Turn me into a great freelance doctor!

481
00:28:59,604 --> 00:29:01,072
Is that the spell?

482
00:29:01,139 --> 00:29:03,641
So did you turn into
a great freelance doctor?

483
00:29:03,708 --> 00:29:05,176
Of course.

484
00:29:05,276 --> 00:29:07,145
I can become anything I want.

485
00:29:09,347 --> 00:29:11,249
Okay, I'll try it.

486
00:29:11,416 --> 00:29:14,052
Abracadabra!

487
00:29:14,252 --> 00:29:17,522
- Turn into Yuming.
- Can she turn into her?

488
00:29:17,989 --> 00:29:19,324
I have arrived.

489
00:29:19,390 --> 00:29:24,329
<i>Spring, distant spring</i>

490
00:29:24,395 --> 00:29:26,531
- Thank you.
- Let me try!

491
00:29:27,065 --> 00:29:29,434
Abracadabra!

492
00:29:29,534 --> 00:29:31,770
Turn into Kaori Momoi.

493
00:29:32,003 --> 00:29:34,572
Why in the world did you call me here?

494
00:29:34,639 --> 00:29:36,775
- It's Ms. Momoi! She's here!
- I know her!

495
00:29:37,242 --> 00:29:39,210
Are you all doing well?

496
00:29:39,310 --> 00:29:44,082
Sorry, but that kind of Yosui Inoue
doesn't fit in here. Please go.

497
00:29:44,149 --> 00:29:46,084
You really are rude, aren't you?

498
00:29:47,085 --> 00:29:49,254
- I've heard that voice.
- Tetsuko!

499
00:29:49,354 --> 00:29:50,889
- Tetsuko!
- Tetsuko Kuroyanagi!

500
00:29:57,228 --> 00:29:58,797
Sorry, it's time for a commercial.

501
00:30:04,602 --> 00:30:07,672
KAZUMA USHIO, DIRECTOR OF
NEXT-GENERATION INTELLIGENT SURGERY

502
00:30:21,019 --> 00:30:23,555
- Dr. Kaji.
- Yes, what is it?

503
00:30:23,721 --> 00:30:27,225
Will you assist me in
Mr. Hachimura's surgery?

504
00:30:27,292 --> 00:30:29,727
- What?
- Me?

505
00:30:31,830 --> 00:30:36,434
I thought you would be
a good partner for me, Dr. Kaji.

506
00:30:38,236 --> 00:30:39,838
Kaji sure has it good.

507
00:30:40,138 --> 00:30:41,472
I'm totally jealous.

508
00:30:41,573 --> 00:30:44,075
I wish I had been born as Director Kaji.

509
00:30:44,609 --> 00:30:47,212
I'm not sure.
I think I have another surgery that day.

510
00:30:47,345 --> 00:30:49,380
He's not going to turn her down, is he?

511
00:30:51,783 --> 00:30:55,119
Please, help me.

512
00:30:56,721 --> 00:30:57,922
I would be glad to.

513
00:30:59,290 --> 00:31:01,226
- Hold on!
- What?

514
00:31:02,760 --> 00:31:04,329
I'll assist in the surgery.

515
00:31:06,030 --> 00:31:07,799
Thank you, Dr. Ushio.

516
00:31:08,299 --> 00:31:12,203
Now then, I'd like to finish
the surgery in four hours.

517
00:31:12,403 --> 00:31:13,605
I agree.

518
00:31:17,508 --> 00:31:21,279
We will now conduct a beating heart
coronary artery bypass surgery.

519
00:31:21,346 --> 00:31:23,581
- Let's begin.
- Yes, ma'am.

520
00:31:23,648 --> 00:31:24,649
- Scalpel.
- Here.

521
00:31:33,524 --> 00:31:34,359
Here.

522
00:31:36,394 --> 00:31:40,465
Daimon, how unusual to see you here
watching someone else's surgery.

523
00:31:41,099 --> 00:31:42,133
What's the matter?

524
00:31:42,734 --> 00:31:44,636
Something is a mystery to me.

525
00:31:45,336 --> 00:31:46,437
A mystery?

526
00:31:46,504 --> 00:31:49,340
What about surgery is a mystery to you?

527
00:31:49,841 --> 00:31:51,609
- A spell.
- A spell?

528
00:31:52,143 --> 00:31:53,344
What's that all about?

529
00:31:55,146 --> 00:31:56,948
I'll collect the artery graft now.

530
00:31:57,782 --> 00:31:59,250
Detaching internal artery.

531
00:31:59,317 --> 00:32:00,585
- Harmonic scalpel.
- Here.

532
00:32:08,126 --> 00:32:11,029
Seeing her standing like that
in the operating room,

533
00:32:11,162 --> 00:32:12,397
she's lovely.

534
00:32:17,502 --> 00:32:19,137
Incising the pericardial sac.

535
00:32:19,804 --> 00:32:22,273
- Here.
- Dr. Ushio, please assist.

536
00:32:23,474 --> 00:32:24,509
- Forceps.
- Here.

537
00:32:34,285 --> 00:32:36,754
The right ventricular infarction is
worse than we imagined.

538
00:32:36,821 --> 00:32:37,755
Yes.

539
00:32:40,058 --> 00:32:42,126
Vitals slightly unstable.

540
00:32:43,194 --> 00:32:45,530
- We must avoid heart displacement.
- What will we do?

541
00:32:49,067 --> 00:32:52,236
- Please take over, Dr. Ushio.
- What?

542
00:32:54,138 --> 00:32:57,108
Please, help me.

543
00:33:00,111 --> 00:33:01,145
All right.

544
00:33:04,449 --> 00:33:06,117
Thank you.

545
00:33:08,353 --> 00:33:11,022
- Lift the pericardium. 2-0 silk.
- Here.

546
00:33:12,156 --> 00:33:13,624
- Forceps.
- Here.

547
00:33:15,994 --> 00:33:18,029
Switching surgeons now?

548
00:33:18,363 --> 00:33:20,098
Dr. Ushio couldn't say no.

549
00:33:26,804 --> 00:33:30,041
- BP is down to 80. Hurry.
- I know.

550
00:33:30,241 --> 00:33:33,478
Dr. Nakayama, affix the stabilizer.

551
00:33:33,611 --> 00:33:34,579
Okay.

552
00:33:51,429 --> 00:33:53,664
What have you done, Dr. Ushio?

553
00:33:53,765 --> 00:33:55,199
- Stop the hemorrhaging!
- Right.

554
00:33:55,266 --> 00:33:56,501
- What?
- Hurry!

555
00:33:56,567 --> 00:33:58,669
Apply compression!
Gauze and adhesive sheets!

556
00:33:58,736 --> 00:33:59,670
Suctioning.

557
00:34:02,774 --> 00:34:05,043
Pull yourself together, Dr. Ushio.

558
00:34:05,143 --> 00:34:06,644
You'll end up making mistakes.

559
00:34:08,713 --> 00:34:11,282
I've had it with you! That was your fault!

560
00:34:11,416 --> 00:34:12,984
What's going on?

561
00:34:13,785 --> 00:34:16,387
I can't take this anymore.
You've always been like this.

562
00:34:16,988 --> 00:34:19,524
You make others operate
and take all the glory.

563
00:34:19,590 --> 00:34:21,426
You don't fail

564
00:34:21,759 --> 00:34:24,762
only because you made professors
who don't fail operate!

565
00:34:25,763 --> 00:34:28,066
- Seriously?
- No way.

566
00:34:30,368 --> 00:34:32,537
Fine. That's enough of you.

567
00:34:33,037 --> 00:34:35,273
- Dr. Murasaki, take over.
- What?

568
00:34:37,175 --> 00:34:40,411
Please, help me.

569
00:34:45,416 --> 00:34:47,452
After you went through all the
American professors,

570
00:34:47,518 --> 00:34:51,089
nobody else would be your assistant,
that's why you returned to Japan.

571
00:34:51,322 --> 00:34:53,191
I heard it from Professor MacArthur.

572
00:34:54,225 --> 00:34:56,360
I won't be used by you again.

573
00:34:56,494 --> 00:34:59,697
- "Used"? Dr. Murasaki, you mean--
- Yes.

574
00:34:59,964 --> 00:35:01,999
I dated her for a year in the US.

575
00:35:03,201 --> 00:35:05,103
I was with her for ten months.

576
00:35:06,037 --> 00:35:08,606
- Can you believe this?
- They've shared her.

577
00:35:16,380 --> 00:35:19,350
I'm out! You handle this now.

578
00:35:20,184 --> 00:35:22,386
I won't be your darn assistant!

579
00:35:23,554 --> 00:35:25,056
Wait! Dr. Ushio!

580
00:35:26,190 --> 00:35:28,192
- Wait!
- I'm out too.

581
00:35:28,693 --> 00:35:31,362
- I'm not going through that again.
- Dr. Murasaki!

582
00:35:32,530 --> 00:35:35,032
You're kidding! Dr. Ushio!

583
00:35:39,737 --> 00:35:43,307
BP has fallen to 55.
What about the hemorrhaging?

584
00:35:43,374 --> 00:35:46,444
- Who's the surgeon?
- Wait! What?

585
00:35:49,213 --> 00:35:53,017
Please, help me.

586
00:35:53,384 --> 00:35:54,719
Impossible.

587
00:35:55,653 --> 00:35:56,621
I can't.

588
00:35:56,687 --> 00:35:58,289
- I can't!
- This is bad.

589
00:35:58,823 --> 00:36:01,492
If this fails, we'll all be fired.

590
00:36:01,692 --> 00:36:04,295
Let's go. Daimon... What?

591
00:36:04,495 --> 00:36:05,429
Daimon?

592
00:36:11,602 --> 00:36:13,337
She sure is fast.

593
00:36:14,539 --> 00:36:17,508
Your spell doesn't work at all.

594
00:36:17,675 --> 00:36:19,143
Bring the heart-lung machine.

595
00:36:19,243 --> 00:36:20,778
- Blood transfusion too.
- Right.

596
00:36:22,480 --> 00:36:25,650
- Method change. On-pump beating.
- Got it.

597
00:36:25,716 --> 00:36:28,653
- Tako, get over here and suction.
- Right.

598
00:36:34,792 --> 00:36:36,327
I'll take over.

599
00:36:39,197 --> 00:36:40,698
On-pump beating?

600
00:36:41,365 --> 00:36:43,100
With the heart beating

601
00:36:43,201 --> 00:36:45,670
and a heart-lung machine
assisting circulation,

602
00:36:45,770 --> 00:36:48,072
she'll rebuild the arteries.

603
00:36:48,406 --> 00:36:50,141
Can she do that?

604
00:36:50,241 --> 00:36:52,076
Repairing hemorrhaging site.

605
00:36:52,143 --> 00:36:53,244
- Lower my loupe.
- Right.

606
00:36:54,412 --> 00:36:56,247
He'll die if you don't
stop the hemorrhaging soon.

607
00:36:56,347 --> 00:36:58,182
- Hurry, Daimon.
- Get it done quick.

608
00:36:59,116 --> 00:37:02,320
Even when I'm rushed, I never fail.

609
00:37:03,354 --> 00:37:04,989
- 4-0 polypropylene.
- Here.

610
00:37:17,702 --> 00:37:19,337
Repair complete.

611
00:37:21,973 --> 00:37:23,307
Thank goodness.

612
00:37:27,612 --> 00:37:29,480
Get that ready.

613
00:37:29,981 --> 00:37:31,482
- Tape the aorta.
- Right.

614
00:37:31,549 --> 00:37:32,483
Right.

615
00:37:40,057 --> 00:37:41,659
- Affix stabilizer.
- Right.

616
00:37:43,060 --> 00:37:44,695
STABILIZER
STABILIZES ONLY THE CORONARY ARTERY

617
00:37:44,762 --> 00:37:46,063
- Hold it still.
- Right.

618
00:37:46,130 --> 00:37:47,298
Incising coronary artery.

619
00:37:47,398 --> 00:37:48,633
- Coronary scalpel.
- Here.

620
00:38:09,520 --> 00:38:10,554
Vitals?

621
00:38:10,621 --> 00:38:14,692
BP, 128 over 83. Pulse, 75, sinus.

622
00:38:15,259 --> 00:38:16,394
Done.

623
00:38:16,527 --> 00:38:18,996
- Nice work.
- Nice work.

624
00:38:25,303 --> 00:38:27,571
- Nice work.
- Goodbye.

625
00:38:27,638 --> 00:38:29,273
We did it.

626
00:38:42,586 --> 00:38:43,587
PRIVATE ROOM B

627
00:38:43,654 --> 00:38:46,490
The heart operation is normal.
The outlook is good.

628
00:38:47,024 --> 00:38:48,426
The surgery was a success.

629
00:38:49,360 --> 00:38:51,462
The prince of the political world

630
00:38:51,595 --> 00:38:54,632
was saved by the princess of
Totei University.

631
00:38:54,699 --> 00:38:58,135
The dramatic scenario
that the people wanted has

632
00:38:58,235 --> 00:38:59,737
come to fulfilment.

633
00:38:59,804 --> 00:39:01,505
Thank you.

634
00:39:02,406 --> 00:39:06,210
- I'm glad I trusted her.
- You're so right.

635
00:39:12,350 --> 00:39:13,617
You're wrong.

636
00:39:14,585 --> 00:39:17,621
It wasn't Dr. Nakayama
who performed the operation.

637
00:39:17,988 --> 00:39:19,323
What are you talking about?

638
00:39:20,558 --> 00:39:23,661
It was a part-time woman doctor
who did it.

639
00:39:23,728 --> 00:39:26,197
Wait. No.

640
00:39:26,263 --> 00:39:29,734
<i>This is the story of
a maverick female doctor.</i>

641
00:39:32,636 --> 00:39:35,373
Listen. It wasn't a part-timer.

642
00:39:35,439 --> 00:39:38,442
- I know about it.
- What do you know?

643
00:39:38,709 --> 00:39:42,513
Totei University has
a part-time woman doctor

644
00:39:42,580 --> 00:39:44,382
with superb skills.

645
00:39:44,515 --> 00:39:47,785
What? Who did you hear that from?

646
00:39:51,555 --> 00:39:54,191
From Dr. Nakayama herself.

647
00:39:54,258 --> 00:39:55,559
- Really?
- Really?

648
00:39:58,996 --> 00:40:02,400
It doesn't matter
who performed the surgery.

649
00:40:03,067 --> 00:40:08,172
For this country,
it's more important who was saved.

650
00:40:09,640 --> 00:40:13,577
I can certainly see why you're
next in line to be prime minister.

651
00:40:14,512 --> 00:40:16,514
You're a different breed altogether.

652
00:40:17,047 --> 00:40:21,719
Dr. Daimon, thank you for saving me.

653
00:40:21,786 --> 00:40:23,454
I won't shake your hand.

654
00:40:24,622 --> 00:40:26,757
I wasn't saving you.

655
00:40:28,192 --> 00:40:30,161
The one I saved

656
00:40:30,561 --> 00:40:32,296
was the patient.

657
00:40:35,599 --> 00:40:37,301
As a doctor,

658
00:40:37,401 --> 00:40:40,104
I'll never be as good as you, Dr. Daimon.

659
00:40:40,171 --> 00:40:42,373
You're not even a doctor
in the first place.

660
00:40:47,611 --> 00:40:49,747
Your spell for not failing was

661
00:40:50,414 --> 00:40:53,150
to put patients' lives
into the hands of someone else.

662
00:40:54,752 --> 00:40:57,121
That's not what a doctor is.

663
00:40:57,855 --> 00:40:59,857
It only harms the patients.

664
00:41:00,591 --> 00:41:03,627
You know,
why don't you quit being a doctor?

665
00:41:08,732 --> 00:41:10,267
I will quit.

666
00:41:10,434 --> 00:41:13,170
- You don't even have to ask.
- What?

667
00:41:14,505 --> 00:41:17,208
I'm going to get married.

668
00:41:17,308 --> 00:41:18,375
What?

669
00:41:20,811 --> 00:41:24,482
She promised to be my wife.

670
00:41:24,548 --> 00:41:26,116
- What?
- What?

671
00:41:28,385 --> 00:41:32,223
From now on,
he and I will save many people

672
00:41:32,490 --> 00:41:34,592
in the political world.

673
00:41:35,559 --> 00:41:37,461
Goodbye.

674
00:41:42,733 --> 00:41:44,134
What's with that woman?

675
00:41:45,336 --> 00:41:47,805
Have a look at this. Look how big it is.

676
00:41:48,072 --> 00:41:49,640
MARRIAGE!

677
00:41:49,740 --> 00:41:51,108
DIRECTOR HIRUMA BROUGHT THEM TOGETHER

678
00:41:51,175 --> 00:41:52,243
I like it!

679
00:41:52,376 --> 00:41:56,313
Incidentally, they're calling you
a god who brings romance.

680
00:41:57,214 --> 00:41:58,549
As a benefit,

681
00:41:58,649 --> 00:42:02,253
we're filled with couples
wanting to be seen by our doctors.

682
00:42:02,386 --> 00:42:04,722
I also secured a promise

683
00:42:04,788 --> 00:42:09,193
from Representative Hachimura
for a heap of grant money.

684
00:42:09,593 --> 00:42:11,662
Congratulations on that.

685
00:42:11,795 --> 00:42:13,297
- Excuse me.
- Okay.

686
00:42:13,497 --> 00:42:16,534
Well... Dr. Ebina is here too.

687
00:42:17,034 --> 00:42:22,406
I would like to thank you
for employing Daimon and Jonouchi.

688
00:42:22,473 --> 00:42:23,807
- This is a melon.
- Thanks.

689
00:42:26,510 --> 00:42:28,178
This is the bill.

690
00:42:29,280 --> 00:42:30,347
- Mr. Kanbara.
- Yes?

691
00:42:30,414 --> 00:42:33,150
Today, I'm in a really great mood.

692
00:42:33,250 --> 00:42:35,386
I'm ready to pay up

693
00:42:35,452 --> 00:42:38,556
exactly the amount you're asking for.

694
00:42:38,722 --> 00:42:40,491
Thank you.

695
00:42:40,591 --> 00:42:43,794
I can see why you're called a god.

696
00:42:44,128 --> 00:42:47,665
- Thank you so much.
- Don't bow to me like that.

697
00:42:49,266 --> 00:42:50,367
Let me see.

698
00:42:52,703 --> 00:42:55,673
- Even this god is surprised.
- May I see?

699
00:42:56,574 --> 00:42:58,742
I'm surprised as well.

700
00:43:00,277 --> 00:43:02,146
It's the price of good news.

701
00:43:02,246 --> 00:43:04,448
I appreciate your cooperation.

702
00:43:04,515 --> 00:43:07,785
Please, help me.

703
00:43:08,452 --> 00:43:10,788
Sorry, but that spell...

704
00:43:11,055 --> 00:43:12,590
It doesn't work, does it?

705
00:43:12,656 --> 00:43:17,194
What magnanimity to marry off
your former girlfriend.

706
00:43:17,561 --> 00:43:21,432
I admire your immense generosity,
Director Hiruma.

707
00:43:23,067 --> 00:43:24,068
That's not it at all.

708
00:43:24,201 --> 00:43:27,571
Actually, I never slept with her.

709
00:43:28,072 --> 00:43:29,773
- You're kidding.
- Kidding?

710
00:43:29,907 --> 00:43:31,542
- Is that right?
- Yes.

711
00:43:31,675 --> 00:43:33,077
- You never slept together?
- No.

712
00:43:33,143 --> 00:43:35,746
What a pity.

713
00:43:35,813 --> 00:43:38,115
She and I were more like

714
00:43:38,282 --> 00:43:41,418
that novel by Hori Tatsuo,
<i>The Wind Has Risen.</i> Platonic love.

715
00:43:41,552 --> 00:43:44,288
- <i>The Wind Has Risen?</i>
- Yes, <i>The Wind Has Risen.</i>

716
00:43:44,421 --> 00:43:47,157
Those two really were a shock.

717
00:43:47,257 --> 00:43:49,660
When exactly did they get together?

718
00:43:49,727 --> 00:43:53,297
- You didn't notice at all, did you?
- Not in the least.

719
00:43:53,364 --> 00:43:55,265
It figures you wouldn't.

720
00:43:55,366 --> 00:43:58,235
- I'd be surprised if you noticed.
- Why?

721
00:43:58,335 --> 00:44:01,538
Face it, Ms. Daimon,
you have zero romantic experience.

722
00:44:01,705 --> 00:44:03,007
What?

723
00:44:03,140 --> 00:44:06,110
- You too, Hiromi.
- Me?

724
00:44:06,276 --> 00:44:08,646
While you two were
rushing through surgeries,

725
00:44:08,779 --> 00:44:11,715
Nakamari brought down the prince
of the political world

726
00:44:11,982 --> 00:44:13,651
with a single shot.

727
00:44:14,184 --> 00:44:16,120
As women,

728
00:44:16,286 --> 00:44:21,158
is it you two or her
who are winners in life?

729
00:44:21,291 --> 00:44:24,561
I'm not about to spend my life
depending on a man.

730
00:44:24,628 --> 00:44:27,164
I don't care if my only mate is surgery.

731
00:44:27,264 --> 00:44:29,633
You two sure are stupid.

732
00:44:30,067 --> 00:44:31,802
If you keep saying that,

733
00:44:32,436 --> 00:44:36,607
Abracadabra!

734
00:44:40,244 --> 00:44:42,780
- What did you say, Akira?
- What was that?

735
00:44:44,415 --> 00:44:46,417
- Hey, Akira!
- Hey, Akira!

736
00:44:47,117 --> 00:44:48,619
Get over here, Akira!

737
00:44:49,453 --> 00:44:51,188
Akira!

738
00:44:51,455 --> 00:44:53,524
Surgeon Michiko Daimon,

739
00:44:53,624 --> 00:44:56,794
otherwise known as Doctor X.

740
00:44:57,161 --> 00:44:59,496
<i>- What rock star?
- Yuji Kudo.</i>

741
00:44:59,563 --> 00:45:01,432
<i>The pride of being number one.</i>

742
00:45:01,498 --> 00:45:03,000
<i>If we don't hurry, it will be too late.</i>

743
00:45:03,067 --> 00:45:05,135
<i>- It's the test results.
- I'm not going to die, right?</i>

744
00:45:05,235 --> 00:45:06,670
<i>Yuji Kudo has disappeared!</i>

745
00:45:06,770 --> 00:45:08,739
<i>I'll do things in my own way.</i>

746
00:45:08,972 --> 00:45:11,842
Stage three retroperitoneal sarcoma.
I had the same.
